      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f71e194626ff47d20bfb43b|full_name}: The problem is that functions having same name behave differently between real-world and virtual-world without any reasons.\nZooming without changing the focal length is corresponding to scaling sensor size or crop center and enlarge in real-world camera. I think that the following parameter combination is the better one if you want to keep degrees of freedom. (In my opinion, focal length and F-stop are enough to the most cases.)\n- Focal Length: it affects both of FoV and blurriness\n- F-stop: it affects only blurriness\n- Scaling: it affects only FoV",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
